[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2713332706","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103947#issuecomment-2713332706","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103947","id":2713332706,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6huivi","user":{"login":"groud","id":6093119,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwOTMxMTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6093119?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud","html_url":"https://github.com/groud","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-11T09:30:46Z","updated_at":"2025-03-11T09:30:46Z","body":"Hi, thanks for having a look to this issue.  I don't think this is the right way to solve it tough. I think the TileMapLayer editor should simply not capture (return true in the forward_canvas_gui_input function) if the mouse-motion event is not used. \r\nI'd rather avoid hardcoded key ID in there if that's possible.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2713332706/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2713466737","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103947#issuecomment-2713466737","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103947","id":2713466737,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hvDdx","user":{"login":"dugramen","id":54819319,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0ODE5MzE5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/54819319?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen","html_url":"https://github.com/dugramen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-11T10:03:22Z","updated_at":"2025-03-11T10:03:22Z","body":"> I think the TileMapLayer editor should simply not capture (return true in the forward_canvas_gui_input function) if the mouse-motion event is not used. \n\nNot sure what you mean. The mouse motion is being used, it's just not doing anything because the pan gesture underneath is panning the viewport\n\n> I'd rather avoid hardcoded key ID in there if that's possible.\n\nAre there input map bindings for it? I tried looking in the input map but didn't find it. I just assumed spacebar was also hardcoded into the viewport controls","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2713466737/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2713521790","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103947#issuecomment-2713521790","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103947","id":2713521790,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hvQ5-","user":{"login":"groud","id":6093119,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwOTMxMTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6093119?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud","html_url":"https://github.com/groud","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-11T10:16:13Z","updated_at":"2025-03-11T10:58:55Z","body":"> Not sure what you mean. The mouse motion is being used, it's just not doing anything because the pan gesture underneath is panning the viewport\r\n\r\nThe `forward_canvas_gui_input` function returns `true` whenever the it sees any `InputEventMouseMotion` event. This function returning `true` means the event has been handled and should not be forwarded to other handlers, likely including the one that handles the pan gesture using spacebar. As a consequence, if this function is modified to return `false` by default, the pan gesture should work again.\r\n\r\nI think it could return something like `return drag_type != DRAG_TYPE_NONE`. That should work most of the time.\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2713521790/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2713677208","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103947#issuecomment-2713677208","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103947","id":2713677208,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hv22Y","user":{"login":"dugramen","id":54819319,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0ODE5MzE5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/54819319?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen","html_url":"https://github.com/dugramen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-11T10:56:35Z","updated_at":"2025-03-11T10:56:35Z","body":"> I think it could return something like `return drag_type != DRAG_TYPE_NONE`. That should work most of the time.\r\n\r\nOk seems to work well. I pushed the change","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2713677208/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized"