user":{"login":"groud","id":6093119,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwOTMxMTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6093119?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud","html_url":"https://github.com/groud","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-11T12:32:16Z","updated_at":"2025-03-11T12:32:16Z","body":"> I just tested on master (without this change) and the Spacebar seems to work correctly 🤔 Did you check if the issue is still valid?\r\n\r\nAh well, I did not :sweat_smile: ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2714007235/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2715021616","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103947#issuecomment-2715021616","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103947","id":2715021616,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6h0_Ew","user":{"login":"dugramen","id":54819319,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0ODE5MzE5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/54819319?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen","html_url":"https://github.com/dugramen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-11T16:40:24Z","updated_at":"2025-03-11T16:40:24Z","body":"Huh, I thought I did test it but I guess not. It works even on the stable branch. Sorry for wasting time 😅\r\n\r\nSo does panning just not get blocked by editor plugins then","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2715021616/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2715765678","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103947#issuecomment-2715765678","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103947","id":2715765678,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6h30uu","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-11T21:39:21Z","updated_at":"2025-03-11T21:39:21Z","body":"I'm curious what led to opening this PR 🤔\r\nI checked in 4.2 and the Space panning still works correctly. I think my comment *might've* referred to wrapping, which would be #54009, so I don't know why I'd assume it's specific to TileMap (maybe brain fart idk).\r\n\r\nBut you came with a fix, which means you did make at least some code investigation or testing (right?).\r\n\r\n> So does panning just not get blocked by editor plugins then\r\n\r\nThis actually might be a \"bug\" from #57000. Panning is handled here:\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/4f0cbc9a58a51f91ddb12af0feeeb96188399501/editor/plugins/canvas_item_editor_plugin.cpp#L1315-L1325\r\nThe method is called independently from other methods, but the `p_already_accepted` is supposed to at least block button input. It's unused now, which *luckily* doesn't break anything (as no editor plugin uses Space).","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2715765678/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2715839420","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103947#issuecomment-2715839420","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103947","id":2715839420,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6h4Gu8","user":{"login":"dugramen","id":54819319,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0ODE5MzE5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/54819319?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen","html_url":"https://github.com/dugramen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-11T22:25:11Z","updated_at":"2025-03-11T22:26:41Z","body":"> I'm curious what led to opening this PR 🤔 I checked in 4.2 and the Space panning still works correctly. I think my comment _might've_ referred to wrapping, which would be #54009, so I don't know why I'd assume it's specific to TileMap (maybe brain fart idk).\r\n> \r\n> But you came with a fix, which means you did make at least some code investigation or testing (right?).\r\n\r\nSorry, I think it's cuz I got mixed up with the setting that lets you pan without clicking. I usually had that enabled in 4.3 but my settings are different in master. So I probably tried panning, it didn't work, and went \"yep its not panning\". \r\n\r\nI immediately theorized the tilemap plugin was probably consuming the input early. The first \"fix\" I tried \"worked\", but that's just cuz it was never broken in the first place. I guess this is why its good to make sure there's an open issue first before diving into a fix 😅.\r\n\r\n> This actually might be a \"bug\" from #57000. Panning is handled here:\r\n> \r\n> The method is called independently from other methods, but the `p_already_accepted` is supposed to at least block button input. It's unused now, which _luckily_ doesn't break anything (as no editor plugin uses Space).\r\n\r\nSeems like a good side effect though. I feel like its expected for the viewport to always pan regardless of the current editor plugin","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2715839420/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]